BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TradeMARK'd Exhibit Grand Opening
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261125T202154Z
UID:682130f08a14f9c97749f6197ce0@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:TradeMARK’d explores how Samuel Clemens became Mark Twain\, 
 and how that identity evolved into something much bigger than the man hims
 elf. Through advertising\, popular culture\, and the curious world of Twai
 n-inspired merchandise\, this new exhibition examines the complicated rela
 tionship between celebrity\, commerce\, and cultural influence. Who contro
 ls a public image? What happens when a person’s name becomes a brand? An
 d how does that image survive long after they’re gone?\n\nSource: https:
 //ctvisit.com/events/trademarkd-exhibit-grand-opening
LOCATION:The Mark Twain House & Museum\, 351 Farmington Avenue\, Hartford 
 CT\, 06405
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/trademarkd-exhibit-grand-opening
END:VEVENT
